        <p>RUNCEMN UNION.-CONTRACTS FOR PRO- VISIONS AND SUPPLIES FOR THE HALF- YEAR ENDING MARCH 29TH, 1902. tVIR GUARDIANS OF THE POOR OF THE RUNCORN • EON are desirous of receiving TENDERS from parties to CONTRACT for the supply ot FLOUR.OATMHAL: ~ .sOcistaccs. PEAS. CHEESE, SALT BUTTER ; COD `IVRIt and PARAFFIN OIL ;QUIRINE: GOOD BEEF. to ~,tosiet of vein pieces Intact, Flat Ribs with Bone, and one .eurid weekly not to exceed 251bs, and 501bs per week of 11115 Best Butcher's Meat for the Officers, and Sides of ,thulton ; BRICAD, HOMB-CURBD BACON, POIATOBS, ,ZREAT, STRAW, DR &amp;PRICY and CLOTHING: Men's omen's, Boys' and Girls' SHOES of various sizes, as per Zun Ples to he seen at the Workhouse, Dutton, and Shoe „etieing ; Housii COAL (Colllerj to be ;timed) ; GOOD tt"'lcAL COFFINS, specifying size, and including plate with e, aRe, and date of death to be delivered In the Union • n and where required ; COKE ; CARTING at per mile ; • NERALS at per Funeral. „ attics tendering for the supply of the above-mentioned inods wilt be required to deliver the same at the Workhouse, 'et of cost to the Guardians. how and when required. ▪ Tenders to be accompanied with samples (except Drapery ods) as fares practicable The Guardians do not bind them- "es to accept the lowest or any tender. Persons desirous of tendering must apply by letter to my • ce, in Runcorn, fore printed Form of Tender (and none • er Can be entertained). where a Schedule of the various articles required and further partioulars may be obtained. Sealed Tenders addressed to the Guardian•, to be forwarded tio the Clerk's Oftl,'!e. Runcorn. on or before SATURDAY, the Ist day of SEPTEMBER, 19:1, endorsed "Tender for' ~:rhs Tenders will be opened and considered at a Meeting ' the Guardians to be laeld in the Board Room, Dutton, on Be 24th day of SEPTEMBER, 1901, at 12-15 p.m. Parties whose tenders are accepted must enter into a iwritten Contract, and be prepared to enter into a Bond with Wel sureties If require