        <p>NTOTICE IS HEREBY GlVEN,that DAVID ARCHER 1.1 VAUGHAN COLT WILLIAMS, ESQUIRE, baviog been appointed one of the Barristers to REVISE THE LISTS OF ELECTORS in Parliamentary Elections within the North Wales Circuit will make a Circuit and bold Courts for revising the Lists of Parliamentary Electors, County Electors and Parochial Electors, and also of the separate List of Persons entitled to be elected Members of the County Council of the County of Chester, though net entitled to bean tip, County Electors' Roll of the said County, for the NORTHWICH DIVISION of the COUNTY OF CHESTER, at the several times and places rollowhag, that is to say : ON THURSDAY, the 12th day of September next, at 10 30 o'clock in the Forenoon, and at 6 o'clock in the Evening on the same day, at the Magistrates' Court House, Runcorn, for the several Parishes and parts of Parishes la the following Polline Districts.v;z :—ASTON- BY-StiTl ON POLIANCr DISTRICT—Aston Grange, Aston-by-Sutton with Middleton Grange, Dutton, and Sutton, HALTON POLLING DISTRICT—HaIton. Norton, and Stoekham. RUNCORN NORTH POLLING DISTRICT—That part of Runcorn called Runcorn North. RUNCORN SOUTH POLLING DISTRICT— That part of Rur corn called Runcorn South. WESTON POLLING DISTRICT—CIifton and Weston. ON FRIDAY, the 20th day of September next, at 11 30 o'clock in the Forenoon, and at 6 o'clock in the Evening on the same day at .the Town Hall, Winsford, for the several Parishes in the following Polling Districts, vlz :—wINSFORD (OVER) POLLING DIS- TRICT—Over. WINSFORD (WHARTON) POLLING DISTRICT—Wharton. ON SATURDAY, the 21st day of September next, at 12 o'clock Noon, at the Town Hall, Middlewich. For the several Parishes and parts of Parishes in the following Polling District, viz, :—MIDDLEWICH POLLING DISTRICT—Bostock, Bpley ; that part formerly known as Croston and Ravenscroit ; Clive, Kinderton ; that part formerly known as Kiaderton-cum-Hulme ; Middlewich and Stanthorne. . .</p>
        <p>ON MONDAY, the 23rd day of S-ptember next, at 10.30 o'clock in the Forenoon; on Tuesday the:24th day offSeptamber next. at 10.30 o'clock in the Fore noun, and at 6 o'clock in the Evening on the sante day ; and on Wednesday, the 25th day of September next, at 10 30 o'clock in the Fore- noon, at the Magistrates' Court House, Northwich. for the several l'ariahes and parts of Parishes in the follow- ing Polling Districts, viz :—BARNTON POLLING DlS- TRlCT—Anderten, Barnton, Bartington, Coashait, Cemberbach, Little Leigh, and Marbury. DAVENHAM POLLING DlSTRlCT—Davenham, Eaton, Leftwich, Moulton, Whateroft ; that part formerly known as the Parish of Whatcroft. MARSTON POLLING DISTRICT _Bud worth Great, Marston, and Wincham NORTH- WICH (CAbTLE) POLLING DB CRlCT4lattford, Northwich ; that part formerly the Urban part of Hartford and Parish cf Castle Northwicb. NORTH WICH (LEFTWICH) POLLING DlSTRlCT—Northwich; that part formerly the Urban part of Leftwich and Parish of Northwieh. NORTHWICII (WITION) POLLING DlSTRlCT—Northwich ; that part formerly the Parish Of Witton-cum-Twambro WEAVERHAM POLLING 'DISTRICT—Acton and Weaverham-cum•Milton. WIN- -I.NINGTON POLLING DlSTRlCT—Northwich; that part formerly the Urban part of Wilmington ; Winning- ton : that part formerly the Rural part of Winnington; Winnington : that part formerly known as Walleracote. And for all and every the Parishes, Townships, and places (if any) within the said Northwich Division of the County at Chester, for which Courts to Revise the Parliamentary Electors' Lists, County Electors' Lists, and Parochial Electors' Lists therein, have not herein- before been appointed. All Overseers and other persons whose attendance may be necessery, are hereby required to attend the sald Courts at the several times and places atoresaid, at which the Lists of their respective Parishes are hereby appointed ta be revised, and all Overseers are required to produce in Court the Rate Books of their respective Parishes, containing the Poor Rates made and allowed during the period between the sth day of January,l9oo, and the 15th day of July, 1901, and to bring with them copies of their Lists, and all Notices of Claims and Objections, and other Papers they have received con- cerning the Registration of Parliamentary electors for( the Northwich Division and County and Parochial Electors of the said County of Chester. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk of th,, Cheshire County Council. Chester, 12th August, 1901.</p>
